1
00:00:08,057 --> 00:00:09,537
Like living in a dreamland

2
00:00:09,797 --> 00:00:11,350
Magical powers gifted to me

3
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:13,477
From the pocket full of treasures

4
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,370
Traveling together across the cosmos

5
00:00:17,637 --> 00:00:19,296
Catching atop the Milky Way

6
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:21,503
The beauty of time

7
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:25,170
Whenever we run into trouble

8
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:30,263
Anytime, anywhere, ideas burst to life

9
00:00:30,676 --> 00:00:33,030
Fly swiftly to a carefree wonderland

10
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:34,980
Hand in hand with starlight

11
00:00:35,005 --> 00:00:37,702
Dancing and shining bright

12
00:00:39,083 --> 00:00:42,643
Step right through this door

13
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:46,597
To make our dreams come true

14
00:00:46,997 --> 00:00:50,624
Crossing over railways and fields

15
00:00:50,797 --> 00:00:54,364
In a flash, the dream express appears

16
00:00:54,724 --> 00:00:55,910
Sha-la-la-la-la

17
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:58,517
Singing along with me

18
00:00:58,724 --> 00:00:59,950
Shouting encores loud

19
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:02,516
Stepping to the beat together

20
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:03,797
Doraemon

21
00:01:03,910 --> 00:01:05,843
Make this moment last forever

22
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:09,917
Our dreams will come true at last

23
00:01:10,297 --> 00:01:11,537
Sha-la-la-la-la

24
00:01:11,717 --> 00:01:13,950
Singing along with me

25
00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:15,490
Shouting encores loud

26
00:01:15,797 --> 00:01:18,087
Stepping to the beat together

27
00:01:18,241 --> 00:01:19,474
Doraemon

28
00:01:19,541 --> 00:01:21,481
Make this moment last forever

29
00:01:21,534 --> 00:01:28,867
The wonderful view will be right before our eyes

30
00:01:31,798 --> 00:01:33,944
"Human Locomotive"

31
00:01:40,006 --> 00:01:41,326
Who's number five?

32
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:43,070
I'm number five!

33
00:01:43,449 --> 00:01:44,459
Lucky!

34
00:01:44,512 --> 00:01:46,141
I'm paired up with Dekisugi!

35
00:01:46,212 --> 00:01:47,812
I drew number seven

36
00:01:51,072 --> 00:01:52,378
I'm number seven too

37
00:01:53,244 --> 00:01:55,144
Looks like my luck isn't so great

38
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:57,225
Get ready

39
00:01:57,319 --> 00:01:58,992
- One, two...
- One, two...

40
00:02:00,372 --> 00:02:01,815
Why aren't you matching my pace?

41
00:02:01,886 --> 00:02:03,608
You said right foot first!

42
00:02:03,648 --> 00:02:05,645
Stop making excuses!

43
00:02:06,572 --> 00:02:08,419
Help me!

44
00:02:11,091 --> 00:02:14,423
Is the three-legged race really supposed to be like this?

45
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:16,316
Hey

46
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:18,110
What are you doing?

47
00:02:18,717 --> 00:02:21,889
There's a three-legged race at tomorrow's sports day

48
00:02:22,424 --> 00:02:25,584
You mean... Nobita and Gian are in the same group?

49
00:02:27,781 --> 00:02:28,727
I'm done practicing

50
00:02:28,768 --> 00:02:30,597
There's no way we can win like this

51
00:02:30,701 --> 00:02:33,047
I was just thinking the same thing

52
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:34,921
I know

53
00:02:35,107 --> 00:02:37,357
You, drop out of the three-legged race

54
00:02:38,627 --> 00:02:39,439
That way...

55
00:02:39,545 --> 00:02:41,472
...won't my partner have to be replaced?

56
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:43,688
What if I don't drop out?

57
00:02:43,818 --> 00:02:46,679
Then you should know what'll happen

58
00:02:47,178 --> 00:02:48,865
How can you be like that?

59
00:02:50,857 --> 00:02:52,939
What's wrong, Nobita? Are you okay?

60
00:02:53,858 --> 00:02:56,738
He said he'll beat me up if I don't drop out!

61
00:02:56,779 --> 00:02:59,282
What now? What do you want me to do?

62
00:02:59,323 --> 00:03:01,544
Gian just runs way too fast

63
00:03:01,628 --> 00:03:02,978
Is there any way that I can

64
00:03:03,018 --> 00:03:05,052
run as fast as Gian too?

65
00:03:05,822 --> 00:03:07,091
In that case...

66
00:03:07,543 --> 00:03:09,557
"Human Locomotive Set"

67
00:03:09,598 --> 00:03:10,524
A locomotive?

68
00:03:10,564 --> 00:03:11,324
That's right

69
00:03:11,884 --> 00:03:14,010
This is called a steam locomotive

70
00:03:14,183 --> 00:03:15,747
It runs on coal as fuel

71
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:18,493
powered by steam generated from burning coal

72
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:20,899
It has tremendous power and bursts of energy

73
00:03:20,939 --> 00:03:22,659
and it's packed with speed

74
00:03:22,699 --> 00:03:23,925
Which, compared to you, Nobita...

75
00:03:24,697 --> 00:03:26,721
is pretty much the exact opposite

76
00:03:28,144 --> 00:03:29,381
Sorry...

77
00:03:30,409 --> 00:03:31,803
Put on this smokestack

78
00:03:32,872 --> 00:03:35,355
Just eat some coal, then drink some water

79
00:03:35,651 --> 00:03:36,395
Here

80
00:03:40,013 --> 00:03:40,991
Here, water

81
00:03:45,807 --> 00:03:46,813
How is it?

82
00:03:47,122 --> 00:03:49,238
Around my belly button...

83
00:03:49,278 --> 00:03:50,730
it's starting to heat up

84
00:03:54,526 --> 00:03:55,477
Incredible!

85
00:03:55,517 --> 00:03:57,518
Power is surging out non-stop!

86
00:03:57,558 --> 00:03:58,705
I can't stand still anymore!

87
00:03:58,746 --> 00:03:59,959
Why don't you try running?

88
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,706
Okay!

89
00:04:05,678 --> 00:04:07,331
This is awesome!

90
00:04:11,688 --> 00:04:12,423
I'm back!

91
00:04:12,463 --> 00:04:14,139
You're back? How was it?

92
00:04:14,289 --> 00:04:15,581
It's seriously amazing!

93
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:17,822
Gian will definitely be shocked when he sees this!

94
00:04:20,227 --> 00:04:21,960
Shizuka, what are you doing?

95
00:04:22,061 --> 00:04:24,491
I have piano lessons, and I'm going to be late!

96
00:04:24,558 --> 00:04:26,756
If I take you, you won't be late!

97
00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:29,043
Huh? You'll take me?

98
00:04:29,443 --> 00:04:30,402
Doraemon!

99
00:04:30,448 --> 00:04:31,228
Alright

100
00:04:37,631 --> 00:04:38,929
Is this really going to be okay?

101
00:04:38,970 --> 00:04:40,128
Leave it to me!

102
00:04:40,537 --> 00:04:42,948
Train, moving out!

103
00:04:45,642 --> 00:04:48,108
How is it? Doesn't this feel great?

104
00:04:50,403 --> 00:04:51,847
There's so much smoke!

105
00:04:52,044 --> 00:04:53,963
What? Go even faster?

106
00:04:54,004 --> 00:04:54,965
Alright!

107
00:04:59,846 --> 00:05:01,151
Are you kidding me?

108
00:05:01,726 --> 00:05:03,242
Shizuka, we're almost there!

109
00:05:03,504 --> 00:05:04,601
Really?

110
00:05:13,274 --> 00:05:14,669
Ah, we're here!

111
00:05:14,709 --> 00:05:16,527
Well? Made it in time, didn't we?

112
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:17,901
I guess so...

113
00:05:18,858 --> 00:05:21,838
Oh dear, my laundry is completely covered in soot!

114
00:05:21,911 --> 00:05:23,144
Mine too!

115
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:24,322
That's so awful!

116
00:05:24,363 --> 00:05:25,195
Tell me about it

117
00:05:26,729 --> 00:05:29,768
I just hope Nobita doesn't get carried away

118
00:05:30,562 --> 00:05:35,142
- One, two...
- One, two...

119
00:05:35,206 --> 00:05:37,833
Hey, have you seen Gian?

120
00:05:38,923 --> 00:05:39,967
Nope

121
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:42,636
We clearly had a chance to take first place

122
00:05:42,756 --> 00:05:44,649
- One, two...
- One, two...

123
00:05:44,947 --> 00:05:45,881
No way

124
00:05:45,922 --> 00:05:47,010
First place is ours

125
00:05:47,376 --> 00:05:48,954
This is the ultimate combination

126
00:05:48,994 --> 00:05:50,916
of good looks and genius

127
00:05:50,957 --> 00:05:53,124
That's for sure!

128
00:05:56,353 --> 00:05:59,354
If that's what you think, I'll show you

129
00:05:59,394 --> 00:06:00,275
Show us what?

130
00:06:00,316 --> 00:06:01,264
No idea

131
00:06:03,444 --> 00:06:05,636
Make sure you hold on tight

132
00:06:05,915 --> 00:06:08,839
Locomotive Nobita, departing now!

133
00:06:11,472 --> 00:06:12,403
Nobita!

134
00:06:12,594 --> 00:06:13,731
Nobita, what's wrong?

135
00:06:13,772 --> 00:06:15,984
- Woah, it's so hot...
- This is bad!

136
00:06:17,662 --> 00:06:18,752
Oh no, Nobita!

137
00:06:18,805 --> 00:06:20,972
- Water...
- Water...

138
00:06:32,989 --> 00:06:34,833
That was awful just now

139
00:06:35,419 --> 00:06:37,483
I need to find Gian right away

140
00:06:37,524 --> 00:06:38,605
Thanks for your business!

141
00:06:39,403 --> 00:06:40,536
Gian!

142
00:06:42,002 --> 00:06:44,102
Let's practice the three-legged race together

143
00:06:44,387 --> 00:06:46,234
Practicing is completely pointless

144
00:06:46,473 --> 00:06:48,374
All you have to do is drop out

145
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,539
Just calm down

146
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,580
Wait until you see how I run before saying that

147
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:03,559
That's it then

148
00:07:04,018 --> 00:07:05,165
Wait...

149
00:07:05,659 --> 00:07:06,788
That's strange

150
00:07:06,984 --> 00:07:08,123
Why's that?

151
00:07:08,164 --> 00:07:10,499
It must be because it got soaked in water earlier

152
00:07:10,699 --> 00:07:13,011
All right, I'll eat up all the leftover coal

153
00:07:13,052 --> 00:07:15,039
and crank it to full power

154
00:07:20,152 --> 00:07:22,187
Nobita, that's very rude

155
00:07:22,228 --> 00:07:23,375
Teacher!

156
00:07:25,371 --> 00:07:26,945
Huh? What is it, Nobita?

157
00:07:28,154 --> 00:07:29,816
N-Nothing's wrong

158
00:07:31,916 --> 00:07:33,741
Your face looks really red

159
00:07:33,781 --> 00:07:35,271
Do you have a fever?

160
00:07:35,779 --> 00:07:36,870
Oh?

161
00:07:36,911 --> 00:07:39,604
Woah, you're burning up! You need to go to the hospital right away

162
00:07:44,406 --> 00:07:45,644
Nobita!

163
00:07:48,455 --> 00:07:49,734
Gian!

164
00:07:50,484 --> 00:07:51,305
Hurry up and...

165
00:07:51,965 --> 00:07:52,953
practice...

166
00:07:53,451 --> 00:07:54,166
practice...

167
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:56,098
You're such a pain

168
00:07:56,983 --> 00:07:58,104
What do you want?

169
00:07:59,652 --> 00:08:01,898
Fine... you win

170
00:08:02,251 --> 00:08:04,341
I'll practice with you for a bit

171
00:08:05,835 --> 00:08:06,796
No amount of practice will help

172
00:08:06,836 --> 00:08:09,077
You can't keep up with my speed anyway

173
00:08:09,624 --> 00:08:10,469
Get ready

174
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:13,801
- One, two...
- One, two...

175
00:08:14,549 --> 00:08:16,442
Looks like you can run pretty fast

176
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,708
I can go even faster!

177
00:08:19,925 --> 00:08:21,321
You're running pretty well too

178
00:08:21,361 --> 00:08:22,885
We can go even faster!

179
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,434
Wait!

180
00:08:29,516 --> 00:08:31,014
Stop!

181
00:08:32,001 --> 00:08:32,874
How's that?

182
00:08:32,915 --> 00:08:35,244
Now you know how powerful I am

183
00:08:36,706 --> 00:08:37,970
So powerful...

184
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,560
I can't stop!

185
00:08:43,424 --> 00:08:45,183
Stop!

186
00:08:45,754 --> 00:08:49,765
- One, two...
- One, two...

187
00:08:50,241 --> 00:08:52,377
- Get out of the way!
- Get out of the way!

188
00:08:54,006 --> 00:08:55,874
- Nobita!
- Nobita!

189
00:09:04,296 --> 00:09:05,896
Hey, Nobita!

190
00:09:06,148 --> 00:09:08,186
Where on earth is Nobita?

191
00:09:08,227 --> 00:09:09,786
Help me!

192
00:09:09,827 --> 00:09:12,111
We can't stop!

193
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:15,820
This is bad!

194
00:09:16,465 --> 00:09:18,456
Nobita, stop!

195
00:09:19,264 --> 00:09:21,056
Get out of the way!

196
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:22,048
It's no good

197
00:09:22,222 --> 00:09:23,956
Cape of Protection!

198
00:09:25,323 --> 00:09:27,410
Doraemon!

199
00:09:34,528 --> 00:09:36,054
It stopped

200
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:42,308
Doraemon, what about Nobita and Gian?

201
00:09:42,726 --> 00:09:44,948
Gian is safe at last

202
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,254
Here comes Nobita!

203
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:54,657
Retrieving Lasso, hurry and catch Nobita!

204
00:09:58,758 --> 00:10:00,010
It worked!

205
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:07,422
- Pull!
- Right

206
00:10:18,955 --> 00:10:20,857
Nobita has gotten so strong

207
00:10:20,915 --> 00:10:23,063
He's basically a runaway locomotive!

208
00:10:24,241 --> 00:10:27,314
He won't stop until all his coal burns out

209
00:10:27,394 --> 00:10:29,291
But if this keeps up...

210
00:10:29,628 --> 00:10:30,622
All right

211
00:10:38,933 --> 00:10:40,611
Wait for me, Nobita!

212
00:10:59,605 --> 00:11:00,669
A person?

213
00:11:01,968 --> 00:11:03,476
Don't run away!

214
00:11:03,611 --> 00:11:05,446
Nobita!

215
00:11:05,713 --> 00:11:07,219
A raccoon-dog locomotive?

216
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:14,046
Don't run away!

217
00:11:17,506 --> 00:11:19,420
So close!

218
00:11:20,731 --> 00:11:21,663
Great!

219
00:11:22,003 --> 00:11:23,721
Stop!

220
00:11:32,709 --> 00:11:35,200
All right, I have to stop you no matter what

221
00:11:46,745 --> 00:11:48,398
Hey, Nobita, stop!

222
00:11:48,439 --> 00:11:50,233
There's a cliff ahead!

223
00:11:52,492 --> 00:11:53,899
Oh no, I can't stop in time!

224
00:11:54,087 --> 00:11:55,598
Not this one...

225
00:11:55,646 --> 00:11:57,178
Something to make the locomotive stop...

226
00:11:58,212 --> 00:11:59,333
This is the one!

227
00:12:07,881 --> 00:12:09,315
Haha, awesome!

228
00:12:11,234 --> 00:12:14,560
(Terminal Stop)

229
00:12:15,532 --> 00:12:17,639
That's wonderful, Nobita...

230
00:12:18,085 --> 00:12:19,170
Doraemon?

231
00:12:19,446 --> 00:12:21,003
A cliff? The sea?

232
00:12:26,978 --> 00:12:28,526
This is so frustrating!

233
00:12:29,445 --> 00:12:30,819
Gian

234
00:12:31,885 --> 00:12:33,478
Woah, Nobita!

235
00:12:33,545 --> 00:12:35,512
Now you know how fast I am!

236
00:12:35,719 --> 00:12:38,252
I'll definitely win first place at tomorrow's sports day!

237
00:12:39,718 --> 00:12:40,699
I'm planning to...

238
00:12:41,425 --> 00:12:42,339
sit out

239
00:12:42,972 --> 00:12:43,743
But...

240
00:12:43,783 --> 00:12:45,899
Save your breath, I'm definitely sitting out

241
00:12:46,434 --> 00:12:47,833
Don't say that

242
00:12:47,874 --> 00:12:49,769
Please, just leave!

243
00:12:49,912 --> 00:12:51,667
There's really nothing to be done

244
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:58,487
"Matsutake Hunting in a Miniature Landscape"

245
00:12:59,287 --> 00:13:01,898
Yesterday I went to a matsutake mountain

246
00:13:03,689 --> 00:13:05,452
Found it...

247
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:06,860
Awesome!

248
00:13:07,788 --> 00:13:09,408
Grilling freshly picked matsutake

249
00:13:10,115 --> 00:13:11,344
over charcoal

250
00:13:11,385 --> 00:13:12,775
enjoying the aroma

251
00:13:17,074 --> 00:13:19,044
and then savoring its flavor...

252
00:13:26,433 --> 00:13:28,270
It's the ultimate treat!

253
00:13:29,030 --> 00:13:30,699
Eating matsutake you picked yourself

254
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,767
really is especially delicious

255
00:13:32,859 --> 00:13:35,706
Why don't you guys try
going to pick some delicious matsutake too?

256
00:13:37,152 --> 00:13:39,353
But you don't have much spare cash

257
00:13:39,387 --> 00:13:40,997
so you probably won't get the chance

258
00:13:45,568 --> 00:13:46,593
That Suneo...

259
00:13:46,634 --> 00:13:49,238
It's so annoying when he shows off

260
00:13:49,278 --> 00:13:51,421
Though it really does make you jealous

261
00:13:51,639 --> 00:13:52,994
In that case

262
00:13:53,399 --> 00:13:55,151
I'll ask Doraemon!

263
00:13:55,315 --> 00:13:58,089
Come on, even with Doraemon's pocket

264
00:13:58,129 --> 00:14:00,268
there's no way he has a whole matsutake mountain in there

265
00:14:00,641 --> 00:14:02,319
Mom, please!

266
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:04,301
Even if it's just once in my life

267
00:14:04,342 --> 00:14:06,509
please take me matsutake picking!

268
00:14:07,962 --> 00:14:10,014
As the old saying goes, matsutake for aroma

269
00:14:10,055 --> 00:14:11,296
shimeji for flavor

270
00:14:11,337 --> 00:14:13,888
Shimeji mushrooms taste way better than matsutake

271
00:14:15,527 --> 00:14:18,725
One, two...

272
00:14:18,847 --> 00:14:20,240
Oh, you're back?

273
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:22,251
Autumn's hearty appetite is such a headache

274
00:14:22,291 --> 00:14:24,014
It's so easy to gain weight

275
00:14:26,508 --> 00:14:29,240
Are you all right? Why the long face?

276
00:14:29,342 --> 00:14:31,573
Mom says shimeji mushrooms taste better

277
00:14:32,741 --> 00:14:34,981
When I really wanted to eat matsutake!

278
00:14:35,021 --> 00:14:37,634
Oh, is that all? That's simple then

279
00:14:37,801 --> 00:14:39,581
"Gourmet Tablecloth"

280
00:14:39,701 --> 00:14:41,348
An all-matsutake meal!

281
00:14:41,675 --> 00:14:43,020
That's not it!

282
00:14:43,061 --> 00:14:44,781
I want to pick them myself like Suneo

283
00:14:44,821 --> 00:14:46,456
and eat the matsutake right on the spot!

284
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,334
What a jerk!

285
00:14:49,783 --> 00:14:52,622
It's so annoying, but I'm so jealous too

286
00:14:53,948 --> 00:14:55,800
What's the matter with Dad?

287
00:14:55,871 --> 00:14:57,329
A friend of mine told me

288
00:14:57,370 --> 00:14:59,395
he caught a char fish this big!

289
00:14:59,461 --> 00:15:00,355
And...

290
00:15:00,755 --> 00:15:01,812
That just proves

291
00:15:01,852 --> 00:15:03,961
there's a huge gap in fishing skill between us

292
00:15:04,001 --> 00:15:06,551
If you won't admit defeat, let's see you catch one too!

293
00:15:08,848 --> 00:15:10,095
It makes me so mad!

294
00:15:11,181 --> 00:15:13,300
If I went, I definitely would have caught one!

295
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,587
It's just that I couldn't go because I was too busy

296
00:15:16,012 --> 00:15:18,720
In that case, why not go to the fishing center over there?

297
00:15:19,310 --> 00:15:20,516
A fishing pond?

298
00:15:20,557 --> 00:15:22,657
But wild char are only found

299
00:15:22,697 --> 00:15:23,857
in deep mountain streams!

300
00:15:24,029 --> 00:15:26,650
I want to challenge the unpredictable mountain streams!

301
00:15:28,273 --> 00:15:31,183
A man's romance is fishing for char in a mountain stream!

302
00:15:34,204 --> 00:15:36,367
Wild char, freshly caught...

303
00:15:36,499 --> 00:15:39,267
...tastes best salt-grilled over charcoal right away

304
00:15:41,110 --> 00:15:42,595
I really want to go

305
00:15:42,878 --> 00:15:43,795
We've got that!

306
00:15:44,813 --> 00:15:46,644
We really have a mountain stream!

307
00:15:46,944 --> 00:15:49,591
"Artificial Bonsai Series: Mountain Stream"

308
00:15:49,697 --> 00:15:52,499
An artificial bonsai? What's it for?

309
00:15:52,539 --> 00:15:54,641
Once you turn it on...

310
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:58,817
...the water circulates to form a stream

311
00:16:01,047 --> 00:16:02,061
Then you put these

312
00:16:02,101 --> 00:16:04,971
Miniature Instant-Growth Fish Eggs into the bonsai

313
00:16:06,859 --> 00:16:08,334
What's going to happen?

314
00:16:11,914 --> 00:16:13,657
Nothing's happening

315
00:16:15,660 --> 00:16:16,735
There we go!

316
00:16:17,042 --> 00:16:19,907
Dad, go get your fishing gear ready!

317
00:16:21,728 --> 00:16:24,181
I've got everything packed and changed into my gear

318
00:16:24,369 --> 00:16:26,148
Small Light!

319
00:16:29,783 --> 00:16:31,635
Hold on tight, Dad!

320
00:16:43,634 --> 00:16:45,006
This is amazing!

321
00:16:45,047 --> 00:16:46,882
And there are so many fish!

322
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:50,356
Have fun fishing here!

323
00:16:50,397 --> 00:16:51,865
Thank you, Doraemon!

324
00:16:52,408 --> 00:16:53,734
It'd be bad if someone kicked it

325
00:16:53,774 --> 00:16:55,699
So let's leave it here

326
00:16:55,792 --> 00:16:58,694
Hey, you said this was the Artificial Bonsai Series earlier

327
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,857
Does that mean there are other kinds of mountains?

328
00:17:00,973 --> 00:17:02,317
Of course there are

329
00:17:02,374 --> 00:17:05,170
There's Rocky Mountain for rock climbing practice

330
00:17:06,594 --> 00:17:08,880
Long Ski Mountain for skiing

331
00:17:09,314 --> 00:17:11,600
Hiking Mountain, perfect for kids

332
00:17:11,773 --> 00:17:14,084
And Adventure Mountain, full of thrills!

333
00:17:15,083 --> 00:17:17,641
With so many mountains, there probably isn't a matsutake mushroom mountain

334
00:17:17,681 --> 00:17:18,685
Of course there is!

335
00:17:18,773 --> 00:17:19,771
Really?

336
00:17:20,418 --> 00:17:23,236
"Bonsai Series: Red Pine Mountain for Matsutake Gathering"

337
00:17:23,277 --> 00:17:24,287
Red pine?

338
00:17:24,356 --> 00:17:26,288
That's right. In fact, typical matsutake mushrooms

339
00:17:26,329 --> 00:17:29,014
mostly grow on the roots of red pine trees

340
00:17:29,055 --> 00:17:31,246
by propagating their mycelium

341
00:17:32,129 --> 00:17:34,235
Sprinkle the matsutake mycelium...

342
00:17:34,826 --> 00:17:37,106
add just the right amount of sunlight and rain...

343
00:17:37,147 --> 00:17:39,166
and they'll grow in about ten minutes

344
00:17:41,039 --> 00:17:41,882
In that case...

345
00:17:41,958 --> 00:17:43,736
We have to invite Shizuka!

346
00:17:45,384 --> 00:17:47,302
You want to go pick matsutake mushrooms now?

347
00:17:47,343 --> 00:17:49,824
Yeah, and it's all-you-can-pick and all-you-can-eat!

348
00:17:50,015 --> 00:17:51,478
Just come check it out first

349
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,450
Small Light!

350
00:17:58,766 --> 00:17:59,865
This mountain is magnificent!

351
00:17:59,906 --> 00:18:00,933
It sure is

352
00:18:01,159 --> 00:18:02,758
Where do you think they'll be?

353
00:18:02,799 --> 00:18:05,627
Let's start searching on the south side of the mountain

354
00:18:05,707 --> 00:18:08,200
Matsutake mushrooms grow more easily

355
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:10,053
in sunny spots with good ventilation

356
00:18:11,183 --> 00:18:13,805
It's so reassuring having Doraemon around

357
00:18:14,809 --> 00:18:16,664
This path is pretty steep

358
00:18:22,817 --> 00:18:24,222
Nobita, are you okay?

359
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:25,710
I'm fine!

360
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,909
Right over there! There are lots of red pines!

361
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,043
Alright

362
00:18:33,078 --> 00:18:35,248
I have to pick them myself!

363
00:18:37,393 --> 00:18:39,035
These are the red pines

364
00:18:39,495 --> 00:18:40,772
Little matsutake

365
00:18:40,812 --> 00:18:42,689
My mistake, Mr. Matsutake

366
00:18:42,730 --> 00:18:44,301
Where on earth are you?

367
00:18:44,558 --> 00:18:46,313
I don't see any around here

368
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,332
Where's the best place to look?

369
00:18:49,482 --> 00:18:51,412
I think it's best to look up

370
00:18:51,452 --> 00:18:54,204
from the bottom of the slope as you search

371
00:18:54,245 --> 00:18:57,256
First check the roots of the red pines, then circle around

372
00:18:57,328 --> 00:18:59,376
They say pine tree roots spread out

373
00:18:59,416 --> 00:19:01,742
over a very wide area

374
00:19:03,653 --> 00:19:05,031
Hey, Mr. Matsutake

375
00:19:05,072 --> 00:19:06,831
Mr. Matsutake, where are you?

376
00:19:11,868 --> 00:19:13,045
Oh no!

377
00:19:13,086 --> 00:19:15,013
Help me!

378
00:19:16,310 --> 00:19:18,417
What should I do? Should I play dead?

379
00:19:18,458 --> 00:19:20,414
No, get to higher ground!

380
00:19:23,551 --> 00:19:24,783
Help me!

381
00:19:25,571 --> 00:19:27,924
Nobita, hurry and get up higher!

382
00:19:27,965 --> 00:19:30,104
Easy for you to say! How do I get up there?

383
00:19:31,889 --> 00:19:33,002
Nobita!

384
00:19:35,289 --> 00:19:36,376
Nobita!

385
00:19:36,417 --> 00:19:38,090
Help me!

386
00:19:38,710 --> 00:19:40,176
Go to the other side of the mountain!

387
00:19:48,706 --> 00:19:49,693
Alright

388
00:19:51,705 --> 00:19:52,975
Caught one!

389
00:19:55,774 --> 00:19:57,326
Where could they be?

390
00:19:57,367 --> 00:19:58,841
Please let me find one

391
00:19:58,882 --> 00:20:00,899
Alright, I have to find one this time!

392
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:03,109
Matsutake... where on earth are you?

393
00:20:03,299 --> 00:20:05,491
He said to look up from the bottom earlier

394
00:20:07,828 --> 00:20:08,713
Found it!

395
00:20:09,242 --> 00:20:10,419
It's a matsutake!

396
00:20:13,581 --> 00:20:14,472
It really is!

397
00:20:14,513 --> 00:20:15,893
-Yay!
-Yay!

398
00:20:16,034 --> 00:20:19,396
But how do I pick it when it's up so high?

399
00:20:22,999 --> 00:20:24,868
Then let's use the Bamboo Copter

400
00:20:24,908 --> 00:20:25,642
You can't do that!

401
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:28,443
Matsutake only taste so good because they're hard to pick!

402
00:20:29,484 --> 00:20:30,478
Nobita!

403
00:20:35,723 --> 00:20:37,722
-Nobita!
-You can do it!

404
00:20:37,868 --> 00:20:39,114
Shizuka!

405
00:20:39,934 --> 00:20:41,561
I'll do my best!

406
00:20:42,426 --> 00:20:44,145
Almost got it!

407
00:20:47,488 --> 00:20:48,455
I did it!

408
00:20:48,496 --> 00:20:49,614
Nobita!

409
00:20:58,052 --> 00:20:59,462
Smells so good!

410
00:20:59,503 --> 00:21:01,989
It's not fair that Nobita gets to smell it all by himself!

411
00:21:05,589 --> 00:21:07,555
What is it this time?

412
00:21:09,653 --> 00:21:10,984
What is that?

413
00:21:19,011 --> 00:21:20,370
Huh, that's strange?

414
00:21:20,411 --> 00:21:22,710
Shizuka was definitely just here

415
00:21:23,142 --> 00:21:24,102
How are you doing, Nobita?

416
00:21:24,143 --> 00:21:25,035
Are you alright?

417
00:21:25,076 --> 00:21:25,876
I'm fine

418
00:21:26,004 --> 00:21:27,648
The matsutake are more important!

419
00:21:27,729 --> 00:21:29,167
Doraemon, look!

420
00:21:29,589 --> 00:21:31,580
There are so many matsutake here!

421
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,739
It's a huge matsutake!

422
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:35,158
They're everywhere!

423
00:21:35,199 --> 00:21:36,805
There's so many matsutake growing!

424
00:21:36,846 --> 00:21:38,499
Mr. Matsutake!

425
00:21:39,352 --> 00:21:41,564
-Yay, so many matsutake...
-There are so many matsutake...

426
00:21:41,605 --> 00:21:42,725
Yay...

427
00:21:44,067 --> 00:21:46,954
What should I make for dinner tonight?

428
00:21:48,936 --> 00:21:50,587
Oh, they have matsutake

429
00:21:54,469 --> 00:21:56,449
T-Ten thousand yen?

430
00:22:00,851 --> 00:22:03,164
Picking this many should be enough

431
00:22:03,738 --> 00:22:05,095
Now then, it's time for

432
00:22:05,135 --> 00:22:08,162
the charcoal-grilled matsutake we've all been waiting for!

433
00:22:08,375 --> 00:22:10,101
-Yay!
-Awesome!

434
00:22:10,142 --> 00:22:13,233
If you wash matsutake too much, they'll lose their fragrance

435
00:22:13,273 --> 00:22:16,345
So just gently wipe them clean with a damp cloth

436
00:22:16,396 --> 00:22:17,985
Then tear them apart by hand

437
00:22:18,038 --> 00:22:20,338
And then you can grill them on the charcoal stove!

438
00:22:20,681 --> 00:22:21,824
But...

439
00:22:22,109 --> 00:22:25,444
I've already prepared some
freshly grilled matsutake right here!

440
00:22:31,702 --> 00:22:33,327
It smells so good!

441
00:22:35,259 --> 00:22:37,564
Mr. Matsutake, don't mind if I do

442
00:22:42,348 --> 00:22:43,909
-Delicious!
-So delicious!

443
00:22:44,094 --> 00:22:45,034
This is what

444
00:22:45,194 --> 00:22:48,121
freshly hand-picked hard work tastes like!

445
00:22:48,674 --> 00:22:51,171
It's truly delicious!

446
00:22:55,286 --> 00:22:56,510
I'm so full!

447
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:57,410
Yeah

448
00:22:57,450 --> 00:22:59,232
Enlarge Flashlight

449
00:23:01,803 --> 00:23:03,591
The matsutake mushrooms got bigger!

450
00:23:03,631 --> 00:23:05,570
I wonder how Dad is doing?

451
00:23:10,383 --> 00:23:12,395
I caught so many fish!

452
00:23:13,061 --> 00:23:14,989
Looks like Dad had a great catch too!

453
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:15,963
Awesome!

454
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:17,529
I'm home!

455
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:18,786
Huh?

456
00:23:20,279 --> 00:23:21,638
The aroma of matsutake?

457
00:23:22,005 --> 00:23:23,332
How could that be?

458
00:23:23,372 --> 00:23:25,871
We don't even have that kind of food at home

459
00:23:29,526 --> 00:23:31,392
-Mom, you're back?
-Mom, you're back?

460
00:23:32,813 --> 00:23:34,181
You're all here?

461
00:23:34,613 --> 00:23:36,514
Look, this is tonight's dinner!

462
00:23:36,693 --> 00:23:38,821
It's freshly picked matsutake!

463
00:23:39,071 --> 00:23:42,215
And wild char that I caught, look!

464
00:23:44,961 --> 00:23:47,818
Matsutake, and... and char?

465
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,902
That's impossible!

466
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,678
I must be dreaming

467
00:23:52,719 --> 00:23:54,971
It's real, you're not dreaming!

468
00:23:55,078 --> 00:23:56,664
Hurry and make dinner!

469
00:23:57,139 --> 00:23:58,825
No way... this can't be real!

470
00:23:58,866 --> 00:24:00,786
Something's wrong with me, I must still be half-asleep!

471
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:02,926
I already told you it's real!

472
00:24:02,967 --> 00:24:04,755
I want to eat delicious matsutake rice

473
00:24:04,795 --> 00:24:07,021
and super savory salt-grilled char!

474
00:24:07,468 --> 00:24:10,845
No way... I refuse to believe a dream like this!

475
00:24:12,568 --> 00:24:14,095
Sha-la-la-la-la

476
00:24:14,155 --> 00:24:16,594
Sing along with me

477
00:24:16,681 --> 00:24:18,034
Shout for an encore

478
00:24:18,088 --> 00:24:20,522
Stepping along together in joy

479
00:24:20,701 --> 00:24:21,914
Doraemon

480
00:24:21,969 --> 00:24:23,948
Keeping this moment young forever

481
00:24:23,981 --> 00:24:30,358
Beautiful sights will come into view

